1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,310
You're at a
crossing when

2
00:00:01,310 --> 00:00:03,400
the men beside
you vanish.

3
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:05,000
The women stay.

4
00:00:05,450 --> 00:00:06,150
Worldwide,

5
00:00:06,150 --> 00:00:06,850
every other man

6
00:00:06,850 --> 00:00:08,750
and boy
disappears once.

7
00:00:08,750 --> 00:00:10,140
You're the only
exception.

8
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:12,410
Driverless cars
keep moving.

9
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:13,450
You dodge
the wreckage

10
00:00:13,450 --> 00:00:15,300
as emergency
lines flood.

11
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,610
At sea, crews
disappear.

12
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:18,250
Shipping stalls,

13
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:20,460
and supply chains
start to fracture.

14
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:23,070
Hospitals lose
staff too,

15
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:24,250
but women
already provide

16
00:00:24,250 --> 00:00:26,320
most health and
social care.

17
00:00:26,650 --> 00:00:28,250
And here's
the catch:

18
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,790
humanity doesn't
need you

19
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:32,120
to father its
entire future.

20
00:00:32,750 --> 00:00:34,710
Pregnancies continue.

21
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:37,390
A boy could be born
moments later.

22
00:00:37,390 --> 00:00:39,750
You're still the
last adult man.

23
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:41,270
Stored sperm
can also

24
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:43,010
preserve other
men's genes,

25
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,320
if clinics keep
operating.

26
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:48,320
Would you help
rebuild, or hide?

27
00:00:48,590 --> 00:00:50,150
Your first
decision matters

28
00:00:50,150 --> 00:00:52,190
more than
your genes.

29
00:00:52,190 --> 00:00:54,040
Remember where
it started.
